{
  "id": "11907_seitei",
  "headword": "{制定|せいてい}",
  "reading": "せいてい",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, verb (suru)",
  "gloss": "enactment, establishment (of laws or rules)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "enactment, establishment, institution",
      "explanation": "The formal act of creating and putting into effect laws, regulations, standards, or official rules. Used specifically for legal and regulatory contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "11907_seitei_ex1",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しい{法律|ほうりつ}が{制定|せいてい}された。",
      "english": "A new law was enacted.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11907_seitei_ex2",
      "japanese": "{会社|かいしゃ}は{社内|しゃない}ルールを{制定|せいてい}した。",
      "english": "The company established internal rules.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11907_seitei_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{条例|じょうれい}は{環境|かんきょう}{保護|ほご}を{目的|もくてき}として{制定|せいてい}されたものだ。",
      "english": "This ordinance was enacted for the purpose of environmental protection.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Specifically used for laws, regulations, standards, and formal rules — not for general \"creation\" or \"establishment\" of organizations (use {設立|せつりつ} or {創設|そうせつ} for those).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{法律|ほうりつ}を{制定|せいてい}する (to enact a law)\n・{制度|せいど}を{制定|せいてい}する (to establish a system)\n・{基準|きじゅん}を{制定|せいてい}する (to set standards)\n・{制定|せいてい}される (to be enacted/established)",
